"false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718320} {:answer/id #uuid "d2c07dee-7197-5236-ae97-50c79044e612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2c07dee-7197-5236-ae97-50c79044e612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718333} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8396714-1f3a-508d-bf9b-07f9d7d01f8b" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf H=(2x\\sin(y^2)+y)\\,\\mathbf i+(2x^2y\\cos(y^2)+x)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718334}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "39a3e7df-998a-5a27-9bd4-ff2ed016c779" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on $\\mathbb R^2$?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Every component has continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. For each field $\\mathbf V=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$, compare $P_y$ and $Q_x$ as functions on the entire plane.\n\nFor $\\mathbf F$, $P=xe^{xy}+\\cos(x-y)$ and $Q=ye^{xy}-\\cos(x-y)$. Differentiating with respect to the specified variables gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=x^2e^{xy}+\\sin(x-y),\\\\Q_x&=y^2e^{xy}+\\sin(x-y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTheir difference is $(x^2-y^2)e^{xy}$. This vanishes at the origin, but at $(1,0)$ it equals $1$. The equality is not an identity, so $\\mathbf F$ is not conservative.\n\nFor $\\mathbf G$, $P=ye^{xy}+\\cos(x-y)$ and $Q=xe^{xy}-\\cos(x-y)$. Now both prefactors depend on the differentiation variable, so use the product rule as well as the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=e^{xy}+xye^{xy}+\\sin(x-y),\\\\Q_x&=e^{xy}+xye^{xy}+\\sin(x-y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThese agree everywhere. Hence $\\mathbf G$ is conservative.\n\nFor $\\mathbf H$, $P=2x\\sin(y^2)+y$ and $Q=2x^2y\\cos(y^2)+x$. We obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P_y&=4xy\\cos(y^2)+1,\\\\Q_x&=4xy\\cos(y^2)+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThese also agree everywhere, so $\\mathbf H$ is conservative.\n\nSelect $\\mathbf G$ and $\\mathbf H$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718319 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c353aa00-6b5c-5d69-9352-5e4af0c311fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718328} {:answer/id #uuid "d0557d28-9769-508c-bf52-ff8cc393ae78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718332}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0557d28-9769-508c-bf52-ff8cc393ae78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718332} :answer-field/id #uuid "04a6888b-7373-5117-aa0d-6b745095a24a" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf H=(x^2+1)\\,\\mathbf i+(y^2+3)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718310} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5caa26ef-4528-52b8-87c9-0ec40c625c87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718318} {:answer/id #uuid "ce65d5e3-fc89-5723-8cbe-76ab7a4ddc0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce65d5e3-fc89-5723-8cbe-76ab7a4ddc0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718331} :answer-field/id #uuid "27ed927b-8d41-55e8-a990-2420e2de942f" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf G=(x+y)\\,\\mathbf i+(y-x)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718312} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e83a7776-faeb-5f4a-a8f4-92e2fd594b1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718336} {:answer/id #uuid "efe81365-2899-5b74-9814-fd46932461b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efe81365-2899-5b74-9814-fd46932461b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718338} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7470c28-774c-5cca-ab54-2215b953157e" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F=(x+2y)\\,\\mathbf i+(2x-y)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718335}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5cbeef57-5154-5e84-9012-6ec66ea66640" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on $\\mathbb R^2$? Select all that apply.\n\nFor $\\mathbf V=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$ with continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$, the field is conservative exactly when $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere. The partial derivatives for the fields below are supplied:\n\n| Field | $P_y$ | $Q_x$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\mathbf F$ | $2$ | $2$ |\n| $\\mathbf G$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n| $\\mathbf H$ | $0$ | $0$ |" :question/worked-solution "All three fields have polynomial components, so their first partial derivatives are continuous everywhere on $\\mathbb R^2$. We can therefore apply the test $P_y=Q_x$.\n\nFor $\\mathbf F$, $P=x+2y$ and $Q=2x-y$. Thus $P_y=2=Q_x$ everywhere, so $\\mathbf F$ is conservative.\n\nFor $\\mathbf G$, $P=x+y$ and $Q=y-x$. Here $P_y=1$ while $Q_x=-1$. These are unequal, so $\\mathbf G$ is not conservative.\n\nFor $\\mathbf H$, $P=x^2+1$ does not depend on $y$, and $Q=y^2+3$ does not depend on $x$. Hence $P_y=0=Q_x$ everywhere, so $\\mathbf H$ is conservative. The components themselves do not need to be equal.\n\nSelect $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf H$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718321 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b1e999d-4854-540e-ae03-e51df1e96157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718315} {:answer/id #uuid "8b9c23dd-0fcd-52ac-99b6-537279f72c32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b1e999d-4854-540e-ae03-e51df1e96157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718315} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8982937-03f2-57b8-9358-2941e8a89273" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf H=\\cos(x-y)\\,\\mathbf i+\\cos(x-y)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718327} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ed0b209-5008-517e-bb17-65871f94428b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718316} {:answer/id #uuid "51785d45-5164-5230-bb17-b7f4334be297" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ed0b209-5008-517e-bb17-65871f94428b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718316} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca0a5f5b-61d9-5d7b-9c3b-60d59f4293bc" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F=(y^2+x)\\,\\mathbf i+(2xy+y)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718330} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28b39f4a-ee9d-501d-b0cc-176c21ec1119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718313} {:answer/id #uuid "85152daf-17b2-57ef-96c7-8981645c93e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85152daf-17b2-57ef-96c7-8981645c93e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718323} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1b84a9d-16f5-5a2d-8d7a-4657cee132fa" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf G=(e^{x-y}+y)\\,\\mathbf i+(-e^{x-y}-x)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718339}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7c1cff4f-ecaf-5c8c-be72-1e859d2c527f" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on $\\mathbb R^2$?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For $\\mathbf V=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$ on $\\mathbb R^2$, continuous first partial derivatives and the identity $P_y=Q_x$ characterize conservative fields. All components here are polynomials, exponentials or trigonometric functions, so the continuity condition holds everywhere.\n\nFor $\\mathbf F$, $P=y^2+x$ and $Q=2xy+y$. We get\n\n$$\nP_y=2y,\\qquad Q_x=2y.\n$$\n\nThe derivatives agree everywhere, so $\\mathbf F$ is conservative.\n\nFor $\\mathbf G$, $P=e^{x-y}+y$ and $Q=-e^{x-y}-x$. The chain rule gives\n\n$$\nP_y=-e^{x-y}+1,\\qquad Q_x=-e^{x-y}-1.\n$$\n\nThe derivatives differ by $2$, so $\\mathbf G$ is not conservative.\n\nFor $\\mathbf H$, both components are $\\cos(x-y)$, but the relevant derivatives are\n\n$$\nP_y=\\sin(x-y),\\qquad Q_x=-\\sin(x-y).\n$$\n\nThese agree at some points but not everywhere. For example, at $(\\pi/2,0)$ they are $1$ and $-1$. Thus $\\mathbf H$ is not conservative.\n\nSelect only $\\mathbf F$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718356 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cd7955a-5547-53cd-be42-ee161381bfb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718353} {:answer/id #uuid "2e0bc149-82be-519a-a52f-35fbac20d37f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718354} {:answer/id #uuid "5e07c8aa-bee8-544e-a53e-44a1fad41ff8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718359} {:answer/id #uuid "c69fb919-839c-5590-bf77-d3f5f99e36c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718369} {:answer/id #uuid "cf8dbcad-63b8-5071-a326-733d7c3d2810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cd7955a-5547-53cd-be42-ee161381bfb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718353} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ae5eefc-b11b-553c-8b05-b62cecb753c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "49775a3a-45b6-53c7-8bde-d92fb5070b99" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n$$\n\\mathbf F=\\bigl(a^2xy^2+(a+1)^2y\\bigr)\\,\\mathbf i+(4x^2y+x)\\,\\mathbf j\n$$\non $\\mathbb R^2$, where $a$ is a constant. Given that $\\mathbf F$ is conservative, find $a$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$. Both components have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. On this domain, $\\mathbf F$ is conservative if and only if $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere.\n\nDifferentiating gives\n$$\nP_y=2a^2xy+(a+1)^2,\\qquad Q_x=8xy+1.\n$$\nThe identity $P_y=Q_x$ becomes\n$$\n(2a^2-8)xy+\\bigl((a+1)^2-1\\bigr)=0\n$$\nfor every $x$ and $y$. Thus the coefficients must satisfy both\n$$\na^2=4\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad (a+1)^2=1.\n$$\nThe first condition gives $a^2=4$, hence $a=2$ or $a=-2$. The constant-term condition eliminates $a=2$, because $(2+1)^2=9\\ne1$. Solving only the constant-term condition would instead give $a=0$ or $a=-2$; $a=0$ fails $a^2=4$. Both identities must hold for the same constant.\n\nFor $a=-2$, we instead obtain\n$$\nP_y=8xy+1=Q_x\n$$\neverywhere on $\\mathbb R^2$. Therefore $a=-2$. The positive square root satisfies only one of the two necessary conditions."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718361 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a1e1cdd-75b0-5146-af64-8ec4cd0d1642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718358} {:answer/id #uuid "79120a4f-28a5-559e-814d-8fc0a69aabc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718362} {:answer/id #uuid "a5db3380-53c0-5006-a630-a2c39361b444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718365} {:answer/id #uuid "b054f672-d77e-5006-bdc8-f715e1ff011e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718367} {:answer/id #uuid "b8198f7e-924d-5741-8bdc-460ee405c22b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a1e1cdd-75b0-5146-af64-8ec4cd0d1642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718358} :answer-field/id #uuid "252c83b7-c47f-51c7-b363-ed7561b81c2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72ad6e07-7ed9-5e47-a681-1c532147506d" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n$$\n\\mathbf F=(2ay+x^2)\\,\\mathbf i+(5-3x+y^2)\\,\\mathbf j\n$$\non $\\mathbb R^2$, where $a$ is a constant. Given that $\\mathbf F$ is conservative, find $a$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$. Both components have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. On this domain, $\\mathbf F$ is conservative if and only if $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere.\n\nDifferentiating the first component with respect to $y$ and the second with respect to $x$ gives\n$$\nP_y=2a,\\qquad Q_x=-3.\n$$\nThus\n$$\n2a=-3,\\qquad a=-\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\nAt $a=-\\frac{3}{2}$, both partial derivatives equal $-3$ everywhere, so this value satisfies the conservative-field condition."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718372 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "370a54d9-d47a-53d0-9bd1-e70b712324ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718355} {:answer/id #uuid "516319aa-eed0-5617-a46a-26d1787580c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718357} {:answer/id #uuid "65204b82-8356-5966-b675-251c38d12986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718360} {:answer/id #uuid "90c9a867-5668-521b-b4aa-a0f651901ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718364} {:answer/id #uuid "a8b0227f-7c3e-5888-9e04-9c172c245f17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "370a54d9-d47a-53d0-9bd1-e70b712324ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718355} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2960c70-b839-5c51-8b0d-0df703c0a5c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718371}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e62e075b-b4da-5871-bcd1-8dac1a69f6e0" :question/problem "Consider the vector field\n$$\n\\mathbf F=(a^2xy^2+x^2)\\,\\mathbf i+(4x^2y+y^2)\\,\\mathbf j\n$$\non $\\mathbb R^2$, where $a$ is a positive constant. Given that $\\mathbf F$ is conservative, find $a$." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$. Both components have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. On this domain, $\\mathbf F$ is conservative if and only if $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere.\n\nThe required partial derivatives are\n$$\nP_y=2a^2xy,\\qquad Q_x=8xy.\n$$\nTheir equality must hold for every $x$ and $y$:\n$$\n2(a^2-4)xy=0.\n$$\nIn particular, at $(x,y)=(1,1)$ this gives $a^2=4$. Thus $a=2$ or $a=-2$. The prompt states that $a$ is positive, so only $a=2$ is allowed.\n\nSubstituting $a=2$ into the derivatives gives\n$$\nP_y=8xy=Q_x\n$$\neverywhere on $\\mathbb R^2$. Therefore $a=2$. A negative square root also satisfies the derivative identity, but fails the stated sign condition."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718382 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37443691-2706-5d21-9d18-4793609e285c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2 x}{2 x^{3} + x} - \\ln{\\left(2 x^{3} + x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718392} {:answer/id #uuid "3c2edd2c-e90c-538a-ba41-aa6e92995369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{6 x^{3}}{2 x^{3} + x} - \\frac{x}{2 x^{3} + x} - \\ln{\\left(2 x^{3} + x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718393} {:answer/id #uuid "de5f25aa-15be-53a9-9859-748400046151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{12 x^{3}}{2 x^{3} + x} - \\frac{2 x}{2 x^{3} + x} - 2 \\ln{\\left(2 x^{3} + x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718411} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d5eed7-8ac9-597b-a25e-a9be998a0d2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6 x^{3}}{2 x^{3} + x} + \\frac{x}{2 x^{3} + x} + \\ln{\\left(2 x^{3} + x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718415} {:answer/id #uuid "f4d9ae32-5cb6-5c08-86c4-54390cb25845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{6 x^{3}}{2 x^{3} + x} + \\frac{x}{2 x^{3} + x} + \\ln{\\left(2 x^{3} + x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c2edd2c-e90c-538a-ba41-aa6e92995369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{6 x^{3}}{2 x^{3} + x} - \\frac{x}{2 x^{3} + x} - \\ln{\\left(2 x^{3} + x \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718393} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e7e4573-6ea1-5b9f-91d6-91e5db661971" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "11412ef8-e1d4-55d5-8834-55ea3b5f02a3" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=- x \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}$ and $y=2 x^{3}$, compute $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ in terms of $x$. Assume $2 x^{3} + x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Since $x$ is independent and $y$ depends on $x$, add the contributions along both paths.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nHold the other variable fixed in each partial derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=- \\frac{x}{x + y} - \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=- \\frac{x}{x + y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $y=2 x^{3}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=- \\frac{x}{2 x^{3} + x} - \\ln{\\left(2 x^{3} + x \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=- \\frac{x}{2 x^{3} + x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the dependency:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=6 x^{2}.\n$$\n\nMultiply along the indirect path, then add the direct path:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=- \\frac{x}{2 x^{3} + x} - \\ln{\\left(2 x^{3} + x \\right)} \\\\ &\\quad +\\left(- \\frac{x}{2 x^{3} + x}\\right)\\left(6 x^{2}\\right) \\\\ &=- \\frac{6 x^{3}}{2 x^{3} + x} - \\frac{x}{2 x^{3} + x} - \\ln{\\left(2 x^{3} + x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718391 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c49b686-f9d8-5c0e-9d8c-ab741240a783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2 x}{\\sqrt{4 x^{4} + x^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718386} {:answer/id #uuid "61d2889e-4e4b-5371-bcc9-7019cc9d062c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16 x^{3}}{\\sqrt{4 x^{4} + x^{2}}} - \\frac{2 x}{\\sqrt{4 x^{4} + x^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718396} {:answer/id #uuid "844671e1-bbd9-5a64-a0b6-914c06c21966" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{16 x^{3}}{\\sqrt{4 x^{4} + x^{2}}} + \\frac{2 x}{\\sqrt{4 x^{4} + x^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718402} {:answer/id #uuid "8e28478f-42be-57a3-8df5-6e61f9fc2b14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{16 x^{3}}{\\sqrt{4 x^{4} + x^{2}}} - \\frac{2 x}{\\sqrt{4 x^{4} + x^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718404} {:answer/id #uuid "c4936fbb-cbdf-5521-baac-ddf6aac99d53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{16 x^{3}}{\\sqrt{4 x^{4} + x^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e28478f-42be-57a3-8df5-6e61f9fc2b14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{16 x^{3}}{\\sqrt{4 x^{4} + x^{2}}} - \\frac{2 x}{\\sqrt{4 x^{4} + x^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718404} :answer-field/id #uuid "af13ab20-80d4-5ddb-b226-630793f29281" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37348ecf-0b0e-57d0-84cf-44dd6e276c64" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=- 2 \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}}$ and $y=2 x^{2}$, compute $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ in terms of $x$. Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Since $x$ is independent and $y$ depends on $x$, add the contributions along both paths.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nHold the other variable fixed in each partial derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=- \\frac{2 x}{\\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}}}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=- \\frac{2 y}{\\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $y=2 x^{2}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=- \\frac{2 x}{\\sqrt{4 x^{4} + x^{2}}}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=- \\frac{4 x^{2}}{\\sqrt{4 x^{4} + x^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the dependency:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=4 x.\n$$\n\nMultiply along the indirect path, then add the direct path:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=- \\frac{2 x}{\\sqrt{4 x^{4} + x^{2}}} \\\\ &\\quad +\\left(- \\frac{4 x^{2}}{\\sqrt{4 x^{4} + x^{2}}}\\right)\\left(4 x\\right) \\\\ &=- \\frac{16 x^{3}}{\\sqrt{4 x^{4} + x^{2}}} - \\frac{2 x}{\\sqrt{4 x^{4} + x^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718397 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32f73266-4a0d-5a2c-8de6-43cef4ed806d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 x \\sin{\\left(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)} + \\frac{\\sin{\\left(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)}}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718390} {:answer/id #uuid "7351e163-b88b-562c-96bf-6649e4f2d0ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x \\sin{\\left(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718399} {:answer/id #uuid "7d873673-55c1-558b-b95f-182ab6aa1e5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 x \\sin{\\left(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)} - \\frac{\\sin{\\left(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)}}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718401} {:answer/id #uuid "8b671f47-1000-5d55-8917-3eeded52693d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x \\sin{\\left(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)} - \\frac{\\sin{\\left(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)}}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718403} {:answer/id #uuid "f162c8c0-88d3-5ee3-b3c3-af2bc1526e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 x \\sin{\\left(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)} - \\frac{2 \\sin{\\left(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)}}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b671f47-1000-5d55-8917-3eeded52693d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x \\sin{\\left(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)} - \\frac{\\sin{\\left(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)}}{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718403} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f641bc0-7716-5c19-b04c-110f39baf432" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718389}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "643ca830-4789-5343-b3d7-0b661d398b97" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=- \\cos{\\left(x^{2} + y \\right)}$ and $y=\\frac{1}{x}$, compute $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ in terms of $x$. Assume $x\\ne0$." :question/worked-solution "Since $x$ is independent and $y$ depends on $x$, add the contributions along both paths.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nHold the other variable fixed in each partial derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=2 x \\sin{\\left(x^{2} + y \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=\\sin{\\left(x^{2} + y \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $y=\\frac{1}{x}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=2 x \\sin{\\left(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=\\sin{\\left(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the dependency:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\frac{1}{x^{2}}.\n$$\n\nMultiply along the indirect path, then add the direct path:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=2 x \\sin{\\left(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)} \\\\ &\\quad +\\left(\\sin{\\left(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)}\\right)\\left(- \\frac{1}{x^{2}}\\right) \\\\ &=2 x \\sin{\\left(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)} - \\frac{\\sin{\\left(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)}}{x^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718398 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "168d939e-085a-56c7-90ad-591a7c0d3d28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x + e^{- x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718383} {:answer/id #uuid "273f6000-dfa7-5212-9b7b-c40cfc38673c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x e^{x} + 1} + \\frac{2}{x + e^{- x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718387} {:answer/id #uuid "95eb68bb-db20-5573-9566-727471d63143" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{x e^{x} + 1} + \\frac{2}{x + e^{- x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718405} {:answer/id #uuid "a9665080-b4d0-5b84-9f30-19919e61c8ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{x e^{x} + 1} + \\frac{4}{x + e^{- x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718407} {:answer/id #uuid "ece1ab51-3655-59d9-bd80-11f51f8b6d2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{x e^{x} + 1} + \\frac{4}{x + e^{- x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95eb68bb-db20-5573-9566-727471d63143" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{x e^{x} + 1} + \\frac{2}{x + e^{- x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718405} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b2e31a2-8d9f-5d40-a044-60341f3b6ab4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "67f18fc3-fe87-5e1c-a70a-b5473f66e961" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=2 \\ln{\\left(x + y \\right)}$ and $y=e^{- x}$, compute $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ in terms of $x$. Assume $x + e^{- x}>0$." :question/worked-solution "Since $x$ is independent and $y$ depends on $x$, add the contributions along both paths.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nHold the other variable fixed in each partial derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{2}{x + y}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{2}{x + y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $y=e^{- x}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{2}{x + e^{- x}}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{2}{x + e^{- x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the dependency:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- e^{- x}.\n$$\n\nMultiply along the indirect path, then add the direct path:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{2}{x + e^{- x}} \\\\ &\\quad +\\left(\\frac{2}{x + e^{- x}}\\right)\\left(- e^{- x}\\right) \\\\ &=- \\frac{2}{x e^{x} + 1} + \\frac{2}{x + e^{- x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718412 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19bc2e70-fdb0-585c-b969-a819e8138795" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x^{2} \\ln{\\left(x^{2} + 4 \\right)} + 4 x + 8 \\ln{\\left(x^{2} + 4 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718385} {:answer/id #uuid "47418398-2406-56a1-b81a-364e81af0627" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 x \\ln{\\left(x^{2} + 4 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718394} {:answer/id #uuid "5844e043-249d-5d10-8a64-c93e6b87b0bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 x^{2} \\ln{\\left(x^{2} + 4 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718395} {:answer/id #uuid "7b46cafe-74ac-5d2f-82e9-6b49f60ad67c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 x \\ln{\\left(x^{2} + 4 \\right)} + 4 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718400} {:answer/id #uuid "be19fe36-0c31-5cf2-a5ae-c2b7186f6b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 x \\ln{\\left(x^{2} + 4 \\right)} + 4 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b46cafe-74ac-5d2f-82e9-6b49f60ad67c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 x \\ln{\\left(x^{2} + 4 \\right)} + 4 x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718400} :answer-field/id #uuid "18eda5e3-c131-5aac-a228-a0885f499010" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e3f2d838-6138-546c-a475-aec46d92911c" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=2 y \\ln{\\left(x^{2} + 4 \\right)}$ and $y=x^{2} + 4$, compute $\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}$ in terms of $x$. Assume $x^{2} + 4>0$." :question/worked-solution "Since $x$ is independent and $y$ depends on $x$, add the contributions along both paths.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nHold the other variable fixed in each partial derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{4 x y}{x^{2} + 4}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=2 \\ln{\\left(x^{2} + 4 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $y=x^{2} + 4$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=4 x, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=2 \\ln{\\left(x^{2} + 4 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the dependency:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2 x.\n$$\n\nMultiply along the indirect path, then add the direct path:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=4 x \\\\ &\\quad +\\left(2 \\ln{\\left(x^{2} + 4 \\right)}\\right)\\left(2 x\\right) \\\\ &=4 x \\ln{\\left(x^{2} + 4 \\right)} + 4 x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718452 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b9e8f39-0933-5a70-8fcd-3ba2f1ed14c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\left(1 - s\\right) e^{t \\left(s - 1\\right)} + \\left(s - 1\\right) e^{- t \\left(s - 1\\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718453} {:answer/id #uuid "35c55a0a-7d62-5af6-ae8b-78fbfae4c006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(1 - s\\right) e^{t \\left(s - 1\\right)} + \\left(s - 1\\right) e^{- t \\left(s - 1\\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718458} {:answer/id #uuid "5193eea8-176e-5b15-83f1-34c0066f0c64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(1 - s\\right) e^{t \\left(s - 1\\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718464} {:answer/id #uuid "7404f69a-8f19-5731-835d-bd3dbbf79255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t \\left(- e^{t \\left(s - 1\\right)} + e^{- t \\left(s - 1\\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718469} {:answer/id #uuid "97856663-0815-57eb-b165-49ba9d08ca0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\left(1 - s\\right) e^{t \\left(s - 1\\right)} + \\left(s - 1\\right) e^{- t \\left(s - 1\\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35c55a0a-7d62-5af6-ae8b-78fbfae4c006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(1 - s\\right) e^{t \\left(s - 1\\right)} + \\left(s - 1\\right) e^{- t \\left(s - 1\\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718458} :answer-field/id #uuid "52aa6935-ad62-5b41-8b0a-3897fa521753" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "061184bf-1fd6-5253-be4f-12bfa4d89df7" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=- \\frac{1}{y} - \\frac{1}{x}$, where $x=e^{- t \\left(s - 1\\right)}$ and $y=e^{t \\left(s - 1\\right)}$. Calculate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}$." :question/worked-solution "![Chain-rule paths to t](images/11/118759b163a4410f66d5855d7b7b1fd9c2ee4be585e778a759997036bd95f765.png)\n\nHold $s$ fixed. Multiply along each path to $t$, then add the two products.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}\n$$\n\nFirst find the outer partial derivatives, treating $x$ and $y$ as independent.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=\\frac{1}{x^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=\\frac{1}{y^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite the outer partial derivatives in terms of $s$ and $t$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=e^{2 t \\left(s - 1\\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=e^{- 2 t \\left(s - 1\\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext differentiate the intermediate variables with respect to $t$, holding $s$ fixed.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t}&=\\left(1 - s\\right) e^{- t \\left(s - 1\\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}&=\\left(s - 1\\right) e^{t \\left(s - 1\\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the chain rule and simplify the products and sum.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}&=\\left(e^{2 t \\left(s - 1\\right)}\\right)\\left(\\left(1 - s\\right) e^{- t \\left(s - 1\\right)}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(e^{- 2 t \\left(s - 1\\right)}\\right)\\left(\\left(s - 1\\right) e^{t \\left(s - 1\\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(1 - s\\right) e^{t \\left(s - 1\\right)} + \\left(s - 1\\right) e^{- t \\left(s - 1\\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "018b5d98-d3c2-5067-b08f-809777a9d4a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 s^{2} \\sin{\\left(t + 1 \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t + 1 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718451} {:answer/id #uuid "1bfa5f8b-1759-5b3d-8188-345d842932e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\left(2 s \\sin^{2}{\\left(t + 1 \\right)} - \\left(t + 1\\right)^{2} \\sin{\\left(s \\right)} \\cos{\\left(s \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718456} {:answer/id #uuid "6b37bf6d-35a9-59cf-8b62-8673e8b4d93b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\left(2 s^{2} \\sin{\\left(t + 1 \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t + 1 \\right)} - \\left(t + 1\\right) \\sin^{2}{\\left(s \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718468} {:answer/id #uuid "b2e1b825-4647-5b6d-ae90-804b43c9e1e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\left(2 s \\sin^{2}{\\left(t + 1 \\right)} - \\left(t + 1\\right) \\sin^{2}{\\left(s \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718475} {:answer/id #uuid "f3c7d1dd-449e-5296-9069-5aabe5cb2e0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 s^{2} \\sin{\\left(t + 1 \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t + 1 \\right)} + \\left(t + 1\\right) \\sin^{2}{\\left(s \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b37bf6d-35a9-59cf-8b62-8673e8b4d93b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\left(2 s^{2} \\sin{\\left(t + 1 \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t + 1 \\right)} - \\left(t + 1\\right) \\sin^{2}{\\left(s \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718468} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2b75a63-d9e2-5de1-90dd-7ecafb125e0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718483}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3f406471-efc8-5921-8251-870eed8ce7bf" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=2 x^{2} - y^{2}$, where $x=s \\sin{\\left(t + 1 \\right)}$ and $y=\\left(t + 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(s \\right)}$. Calculate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}$." :question/worked-solution "![Chain-rule paths to t](images/11/118759b163a4410f66d5855d7b7b1fd9c2ee4be585e778a759997036bd95f765.png)\n\nHold $s$ fixed. Multiply along each path to $t$, then add the two products.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}\n$$\n\nFirst find the outer partial derivatives, treating $x$ and $y$ as independent.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=4 x, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=- 2 y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite the outer partial derivatives in terms of $s$ and $t$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=4 s \\sin{\\left(t + 1 \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=- 2 \\left(t + 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(s \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext differentiate the intermediate variables with respect to $t$, holding $s$ fixed.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t}&=s \\cos{\\left(t + 1 \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}&=\\sin{\\left(s \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the chain rule and simplify the products and sum.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}&=\\left(4 s \\sin{\\left(t + 1 \\right)}\\right)\\left(s \\cos{\\left(t + 1 \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(- 2 \\left(t + 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(s \\right)}\\right)\\left(\\sin{\\left(s \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=2 \\left(2 s^{2} \\sin{\\left(t + 1 \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t + 1 \\right)} - \\left(t + 1\\right) \\sin^{2}{\\left(s \\right)}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718476 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ad8b6b8-c988-5a2a-913f-88a620e8ef6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(s - 1\\right) \\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) e^{\\left(s - 1\\right) \\left(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718455} {:answer/id #uuid "2a286ed4-8ada-51d3-bc99-e617ec2ad7a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(s - 1\\right) \\left(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) e^{\\left(s - 1\\right) \\left(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718457} {:answer/id #uuid "45b07bce-e792-5466-8242-e79c841d5991" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(s - 1\\right) \\left(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) e^{\\left(s - 1\\right) \\left(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718462} {:answer/id #uuid "7c543aad-39e0-5baf-a989-3c7131c175a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\left(s - 1\\right) e^{\\left(s - 1\\right) \\left(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718471} {:answer/id #uuid "7d21aea1-86e1-5ba3-8f26-b0cb26a0b6c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(s - 1\\right) e^{\\left(s - 1\\right) \\left(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a286ed4-8ada-51d3-bc99-e617ec2ad7a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(s - 1\\right) \\left(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) e^{\\left(s - 1\\right) \\left(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718457} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ef825dd-b695-53ef-9748-c3c2be9610ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718454}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b3a3bd41-91a5-5917-a36d-5d642d4ed8c4" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=e^{x + y}$, where $x=\\left(s - 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=\\left(s - 1\\right) \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}$. Calculate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}$." :question/worked-solution "![Chain-rule paths to t](images/11/118759b163a4410f66d5855d7b7b1fd9c2ee4be585e778a759997036bd95f765.png)\n\nHold $s$ fixed. Multiply along each path to $t$, then add the two products.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}\n$$\n\nFirst find the outer partial derivatives, treating $x$ and $y$ as independent.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=e^{x + y}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=e^{x + y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite the outer partial derivatives in terms of $s$ and $t$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=e^{\\left(s - 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\left(s - 1\\right) \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=e^{\\left(s - 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\left(s - 1\\right) \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext differentiate the intermediate variables with respect to $t$, holding $s$ fixed.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t}&=\\left(s - 1\\right) \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}&=- \\left(s - 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the chain rule and simplify the products and sum.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}&=\\left(e^{\\left(s - 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\left(s - 1\\right) \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}}\\right)\\left(\\left(s - 1\\right) \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(e^{\\left(s - 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\left(s - 1\\right) \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}}\\right)\\left(- \\left(s - 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=\\left(s - 1\\right) \\left(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) e^{\\left(s - 1\\right) \\left(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3af654b2-b4db-51c2-b4e1-b32be3b609f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(\\left(t + 1\\right) e^{s} + 2\\right) e^{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718459} {:answer/id #uuid "52a1f530-500b-5a25-aa75-529eaa436b7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 s e^{2 s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718465} {:answer/id #uuid "76b9f946-3c8e-5701-bb85-48f427f9ddb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718470} {:answer/id #uuid "8dc8a6d7-0bee-57e9-9a26-6209f3e9a401" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(s \\left(t + 1\\right) e^{s} + \\left(s + 1\\right) \\left(\\left(t + 1\\right) e^{s} + 2\\right)\\right) e^{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718473} {:answer/id #uuid "d85363b3-a85e-581b-b972-602bc1737457" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s e^{2 s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d85363b3-a85e-581b-b972-602bc1737457" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s e^{2 s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718482} :answer-field/id #uuid "54908566-9a70-5e3a-a4e8-504f0f4c4bde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718467}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c0ff74da-7d5b-58c5-aff7-0c4dd6e7fe50" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=x y + 2 y$, where $x=\\left(t + 1\\right) e^{s}$ and $y=s e^{s}$. Calculate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}$." :question/worked-solution "![Chain-rule paths to t](images/11/118759b163a4410f66d5855d7b7b1fd9c2ee4be585e778a759997036bd95f765.png)\n\nHold $s$ fixed. Multiply along each path to $t$, then add the two products.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}\n$$\n\nFirst find the outer partial derivatives, treating $x$ and $y$ as independent.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=y, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=x + 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite the outer partial derivatives in terms of $s$ and $t$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=s e^{s}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=\\left(t + 1\\right) e^{s} + 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext differentiate the intermediate variables with respect to $t$, holding $s$ fixed.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial t}&=e^{s}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial t}&=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the chain rule and simplify the products and sum.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}&=\\left(s e^{s}\\right)\\left(e^{s}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(\\left(t + 1\\right) e^{s} + 2\\right)\\left(0\\right) \\\\ &=s e^{2 s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718481 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f319d94-3c40-5d49-9cbe-cc70c3e3a7a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (\\sin{\\left(t + 1 \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t + 1 \\right)})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718463} {:answer/id #uuid "bfd5ce86-1460-588f-8878-8b1b07d24473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\left(s + 1\\right) \\cos{\\left(t + 1 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718477} {:answer/id #uuid "c04c71d8-b7c1-5140-a07e-2eed7d45cb62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\sin{\\left(t + 1 \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t + 1 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718478} {:answer/id #uuid "ccc26ac6-fd05-5404-b541-0b269861c4cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718480} {:answer/id #uuid "f4182d90-3c42-5a78-b637-f950c7d2b01c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s \\sin^{2}{\\left(t + 1 \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(t + 1 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f319d94-3c40-5d49-9cbe-cc70c3e3a7a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (\\sin{\\left(t + 1 \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t + 1 \\right)})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718463} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c88b3d4-b2b3-5004-9e30-21092d39bd74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd7f2dcc-d5af-584d-92bc-8bff5969d9f9" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y)=x - y$, where $x=- s \\cos{\\left(t + 1 \\right)}$ and $y=s \\sin{\\left(t + 1 \\right)}$. Calculate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}$." :question/worked-solution "![Chain-rule paths to s](images/21/21cec766fe72965697304ef4288ffb2b090ddfca179210165dbcfd42ec490b27.png)\n\nHold $t$ fixed. Multiply along each path to $s$, then add the two products.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial s}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial s}\n$$\n\nFirst find the outer partial derivatives, treating $x$ and $y$ as independent.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=1, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite the outer partial derivatives in terms of $s$ and $t$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=1, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext differentiate the intermediate variables with respect to $s$, holding $t$ fixed.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial s}&=- \\cos{\\left(t + 1 \\right)}, \\\\ \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial s}&=\\sin{\\left(t + 1 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute into the chain rule and simplify the products and sum.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}&=\\left(1\\right)\\left(- \\cos{\\left(t + 1 \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &\\quad {}+\\left(-1\\right)\\left(\\sin{\\left(t + 1 \\right)}\\right) \\\\ &=- (\\sin{\\left(t + 1 \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t + 1 \\right)}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718523 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "427b0f1f-73de-5a0a-8fe3-a671f8cb1b2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718545} {:answer/id #uuid "bf293c2b-0096-5fbf-b4c1-9886c199c7a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718573}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "427b0f1f-73de-5a0a-8fe3-a671f8cb1b2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860454