fficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "33c3e1ea-37e8-55ff-aca9-27c31daffdc4" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on $\\mathbb R^2$? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "All components have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. Polynomial, exponential, trigonometric and arctangent functions are smooth here; any logarithm has positive argument and any denominator is strictly positive. Thus $\\mathbf V=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$ is **conservative** exactly when $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere.\n\nFor $\\mathbf F$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=2 e^{x - y} - 1,\\\\Q&=- e^{x - y} - 1,\\\\P_y&=- 2 e^{x - y},\\\\Q_x&=- e^{x - y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivatives are not equal everywhere, so $\\mathbf F$ is not conservative. At $(0,0)$, the difference is $-1\\ne0$.\n\nFor $\\mathbf G$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=- 2 y e^{2 x} + 1,\\\\Q&=- 2 y - e^{2 x},\\\\P_y&=- 2 e^{2 x},\\\\Q_x&=- 2 e^{2 x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$P_y=Q_x$ is an identity, so $\\mathbf G$ is conservative.\n\nFor $\\mathbf H$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=2 \\cos{\\left(2 x + y \\right)} + 1,\\\\Q&=3 \\cos{\\left(2 x + y \\right)},\\\\P_y&=- 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x + y \\right)},\\\\Q_x&=- 6 \\sin{\\left(2 x + y \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivatives are not equal everywhere, so $\\mathbf H$ is not conservative. At $(1,0)$, the difference is $4 \\sin{\\left(2 \\right)}\\ne0$.\n\nSelect $\\mathbf G$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718544 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1de9ecd9-755e-559b-be8b-e5a181485001" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718532} {:answer/id #uuid "849d8186-dc4b-59f4-8e05-985e62a56146" :answer/type {:db/id #ed