icated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=- 2 y e^{2 x} + 1,\\\\Q&=y + e^{2 x},\\\\P_y&=- 2 e^{2 x},\\\\Q_x&=2 e^{2 x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivatives are not equal everywhere, so $\\mathbf H$ is not conservative. At $(0,0)$, the difference is $-4\\ne0$.\n\nSelect $\\mathbf F$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718663 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12e85579-1731-5649-a193-1bc8b20e53a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718659} {:answer/id #uuid "2748dde3-4ed6-5915-9e47-5edec3e27f4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2748dde3-4ed6-5915-9e47-5edec3e27f4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718662} :answer-field/id #uuid "0222e3af-101b-5582-99e1-672294303965" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F=$ $\\left(- 2 y e^{2 x y} + \\cos{\\left(x - y \\right)} + 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf i$ $+\\left(x e^{2 x y} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x - y \\right)} - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718654} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95214e7b-72a7-5c71-81eb-4ae4ac1c597a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718686} {:answer/id #uuid "b3a20c97-46a9-5220-a6be-7ff52d90ee0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718692}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95214e7b-72a7-5c71-81eb-4ae4ac1c597a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718686} :answer-field/id #uuid "71d1c6b7-ddc2-540e-93ee-2e060e0ffec6" :answer-fie