db/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718701}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "29ecce45-7e33-5bcb-a6a9-f04f2dea6e47" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on $\\mathbb R^2$? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "All components have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. Polynomial, exponential, trigonometric and arctangent functions are smooth here; any logarithm has positive argument and any denominator is strictly positive. Thus $\\mathbf V=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$ is **conservative** exactly when $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere.\n\nFor $\\mathbf F$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=- 2 y e^{2 x y} + \\cos{\\left(x - y \\right)} + 1,\\\\Q&=x e^{2 x y} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x - y \\right)} - 1,\\\\P_y&=- 4 x y e^{2 x y} - 2 e^{2 x y} + \\sin{\\left(x - y \\right)},\\\\Q_x&=2 x y e^{2 x y} + e^{2 x y} - 3 \\sin{\\left(x - y \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivatives are not equal everywhere, so $\\mathbf F$ is not conservative. At $(0,0)$, the difference is $-3\\ne0$.\n\nFor $\\mathbf G$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=4 x \\sin{\\left(y^{2} \\right)} - y + 1,\\\\Q&=- 6 x^{2} y \\cos{\\left(y^{2} \\right)} - x + 1,\\\\P_y&=8 x y \\cos{\\left(y^{2} \\right)} - 1,\\\\Q_x&=- 12 x y \\cos{\\left(y^{2} \\right)} - 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivatives are not equal everywhere, so $\\mathbf G$ is not conservative. At $(1,1)$, the difference is $20 \\cos{\\left(1 \\right)}\\ne0$.\n\nFor $\\mathbf H$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=y e^{x y} + \\cos{\\left(x - y \\right)} - 1,\\\\Q&=3 x e^{x y} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x - y \\right)} - 1,\\\\P_y&=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y} + \\sin{\\left(x - y \\right)},\\\\Q_x&=3 x y e^{x y} + 3 e^{x y} - 3 \\sin{\\left(x - y \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivatives are not equal everywhere, so $\\mathbf H$ is not conservative. At $(0,0)$, the difference is $-2\\ne0$.\n\nSelect **None of the above**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718666 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "460e7fa9-356f-54f7-944f-7c1ee15722e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718670} {:answer/id #uuid "5d6fb9d6-ae2e-5bf9-b095-478b2bf1f03f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d6fb9d6-ae2e-5bf9-b095-478b2bf1f03f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718675} :answer-field/id #uuid "491dd3bc-654e-59fa-96e5-65a77535fe91" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf G=$ $\\left(- y \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)} + 2 y - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf i$ $+\\left(- x \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)} + x\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718671} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d2db9bb-a6ea-5480-a052-2a1b96c7df39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718674} {:answer/id #uuid "81e9a346-8b99-5485-96db-b365d48a95a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d2db9bb-a6ea-5480-a052-2a1b96c7df39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718674} :answer-field/id #uuid "d757898e-419e-5fcd-bb1a-bcddb3d2a0e1" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 