tion/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "302ddd5e-b216-5521-92cd-7a2eb9f1bd86" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on $\\mathbb R^2$? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "All components have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. Polynomial, exponential, trigonometric and arctangent functions are smooth here; any logarithm has positive argument and any denominator is strictly positive. Thus $\\mathbf V=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$ is **conservative** exactly when $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere.\n\nFor $\\mathbf F$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=- 2 x \\sin{\\left(y^{2} \\right)} + 2 y + 1,\\\\Q&=- 2 x^{2} y \\cos{\\left(y^{2} \\right)} + 2 x,\\\\P_y&=- 4 x y \\cos{\\left(y^{2} \\right)} + 2,\\\\Q_x&=- 4 x y \\cos{\\left(y^{2} \\right)} + 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$P_y=Q_x$ is an identity, so $\\mathbf F$ is conservative.\n\nFor $\\mathbf G$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=- y \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)} + 2 y - 1,\\\\Q&=- x \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)} + x,\\\\P_y&=x y \\sin{\\left(x y \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)} + 2,\\\\Q_x&=x y \\sin{\\left(x y \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)} + 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivatives are not equal everywhere, so $\\mathbf G$ is not conservative. At $(0,0)$, the difference is $1\\ne0$.\n\nFor $\\mathbf H$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=- y \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)} + 2 y,\\\\Q&=2 x \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)} - 1,\\\\P_y&=x y \\sin{\\left(x y \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)} + 2,\\\\Q_x&=- 2 x y \\sin{\\left(x y \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(x y \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivatives are not equal everywhere, so $\\mathbf H$ is not conservative. At $(0,0)$, the difference is $-1\\ne0$.\n\nSelect $\\mathbf F$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718681 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "148859ae-2528-50b0-b57c-3587d3e6d5b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718660} {:answer/id #uuid "c50d9b11-2d54-5607-bea1-e8cb3c3cc812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "148859ae-2528-50b0-b57c-3587d3e6d5b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718660} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e3417d3-9544-57b7-bf9b-e3647bbec23d" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf H=$ $\\left(- 4 x \\sin{\\left(y^{2} \\right)} - y - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf i$ $+\\left(- 4 x^{2} y \\cos{\\left(y^{2} \\right)} - x\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718685} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "846f2cfc-5098-5368-a71b-da7ab7542fce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718682} {:answer/id #uuid "af955189-81de-5c12-acc0-44eef08eb9fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af955189-81de-5c12-acc0-44eef08eb9fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718691} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7c05d34-f52b-5e91-bdf6-688a6d763ce8" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf G=$ $\\left(- 2 x \\sin{\\left(y^{2} \\right)} - 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf i$ $+\\left(- 2 x - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718694} {:answer-field/choices [{: