alue "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7524397a-c53d-5b50-957b-30e07220eb80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718677} :answer-field/id #uuid "d39de1ad-a4d7-555e-9617-e4404a9de48e" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf H=$ $\\left(y e^{2 x y} + \\cos{\\left(x - y \\right)} - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf i$ $+\\left(x e^{2 x y} - \\cos{\\left(x - y \\right)} - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718696} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4302ed5e-f7cd-5fe6-86d6-89086faabad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718669} {:answer/id #uuid "4efbb189-90d3-50b2-b0e4-f4cbec08ed5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4efbb189-90d3-50b2-b0e4-f4cbec08ed5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718672} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7ddf8be-da44-500a-8380-619b4526e7d9" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aeecebd8-1743-59be-a7be-044dca376a2c" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on $\\mathbb R^2$? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "All components have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. Polynomial, exponential, trigonometric and arctangent functions are smooth here; any logarithm has positive argument and any denominator is strictly positive. Thus $\\mathbf V=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$ is **conservative** exactly when $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere.\n\nFor $\\mathbf F$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=- 4 x \\sin{\\left(y^{2} \\right)} + y - 1,\\\\Q&=- 4 x^{2} y \\cos{\\left(y^{2} \\right)} + x,\\\\P_y&=- 8 x y \\cos{\\left(y^{2} \\right)} + 1,\\\\Q_x&=- 8 x y \\cos{\\left(y^{2} \\right)} + 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$P_y=Q_x$ is an identity, so $\\mathbf F$ is conservative.\n\nFor $\\mathbf G$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=2 y \\cos{\\left(2 x y \\right)} + 2 y + 1,\\\\Q&=2 x \\cos{\\left(2 x y \\right)} + 2 x,\\\\P_y&=- 4 x y \\sin{\\left(2 x y \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(2 x y \\right)} + 2,\\\\Q_x&=- 4 x y \\sin{\\left(2 x y \\right)} + 2 \\cos{\\left(2 x y \\right)} + 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$P_y=Q_x$ is an identity, so $\\mathbf G$ is conservative.\n\nFor $\\mathbf H$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=y e^{2 x y} + \\cos{\\left(x - y \\right)} - 1,\\\\Q&=x e^{2 x y} - \\cos{\\left(x - y \\right)} - 1,\\\\P_y&=2 x y e^{2 x y} + e^{2 x y} + \\sin{\\left(x - y \\right)},\\\\Q_x&=2 x y e^{2 x y} + e^{2 x y} + \\sin{\\left(x - y \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$P_y=Q_x$ is an identity, so $\\mathbf H$ is conservative.\n\nSelect $\\mathbf F$, $\\mathbf G$, $\\mathbf H$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718717 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43915801-5bf4-5df3-977d-9f314eb9e71c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718720} {:answer/id #uuid "aedec94c-3549-5bff-985a-d8d686c5c8f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aedec94c-3549-5bff-985a-d8d686c5c8f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718743} :answer-field/id #uuid "12a2481f-813f-5e10-83f2-79104ec410ba" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf H=$ $\\left(4 x y^{2} + 2 x + 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf i$ $+\\left(- 6 x^{2} y + 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718710} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b7b97d6-6d6b-547e-8cca-dd92643581eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718722} {:answer/id #uuid "6f0f70cc-b0e6-5746-abb5-31fcd15857e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b7b97d6-6d6b-547e-8cca-dd92643581eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718722} :answer-field/id #uuid "27a35ac9-667d-5195-b620-1f1df56ce9c2" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F=$ $\\left(x - y - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf i$ $+\\left(- 2 x + y - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718715} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6204ecee-e0fe-54e1-b916-0aa0422aed03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718726} {:answer/id #uuid "e82d43f9-0f8c-5a4f-a8a9-85e2e6cccaa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e82d43f9-0f8c-5a4f-a8a9-85e2e6cccaa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718752} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fedbcb6-887e-55d1-9796-d8f4a0a66836" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718733} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70f257b9-aca1-50d8-b6a5-697fea9b513a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718730} {:answer/id #uuid "9104c683-c2b0-5750-83c9-3744b814aee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9104c683-c2b0-5750-83c9-3744b814aee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718734} :answer-field/id #uuid "bce53f3d-f766-59ca-bf42-0ed629dad6d1" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf G=$ $\\left(- 2 x - 2 y - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf i$ $+\\left(- 2 x - 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718744}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3afd4609-5600-55a1-b2ca-e66ec3f5687f" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on $\\mathbb R^2$? Select all that apply.\n\nFor $\\mathbf V=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$ with continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$, the field is conservative exactly when $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere. The partial derivatives are supplied:\n\n| Field | $P_y$ | $Q_x$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\mathbf F$ | $-1$ | $-2$ |\n| $\\mathbf G$ | $-2$ | $-2$ |\n| $\\mathbf H$ | $8 x y$ | $- 12 x y$ |" :question/worked-solution "All components have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. Polynomial, exponential, trigonometric and arctangent functions are smooth here; any logarithm has positive argument and any denominator is strictly positive. Thus $\\mathbf V=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$ is **conservative** exactly when $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere.\n\nFor $\\mathbf F$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=x - y - 1,\\\\Q&=- 2 x + y - 1,\\\\P_y&=-1,\\\\Q_x&=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivatives are not equal everywhere, so $\\mathbf F$ is not conservative. At $(0,0)$, the difference is $1\\ne0$.\n\nFor $\\mathbf G$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=- 2 x - 2 y - 1,\\\\Q&=- 2 x - 2 y,\\\\P_y&=-2,\\\\Q_x&=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$P_y=Q_x$ is an identity, so $\\mathbf G$ is conservative.\n\nFor $\\mathbf H$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=4 x y^{2} + 2 x + 1,\\\\Q&=- 6 x^{2} y + 2 y,\\\\P_y&=8 x y,\\\\Q_x&=- 12 x y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivatives are not equal everywhere, so $\\mathbf H$ is not conservative. At $(1,1)$, the difference is $20\\ne0$.\n\nSelect $\\mathbf G$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718718 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fbd3439-ed8d-533b-a871-dbba6fe43244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718724} {:answer/id #uuid "99c524e3-fb98-5a15-b2b7-ec27c71f7f42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fbd3439-ed8d-533b-a871-dbba6fe43244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718724} :answer-field/id #uuid "94cb7d70-bbb1-52e8-bf81-a2ca04923410" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf G=$ $\\left(2 x y + 2 x\\right)\\,\\mathbf i$ $+\\left(- x^{2} + 2 y - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718735} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20ccf95e-b504-5f7b-9454-9eb6bd0604c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718714} {:answer/id #uuid "5e5f5970-a44c-5a92-afd2-3862e66239d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e5f5970-a44c-5a92-afd2-3862e66239d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718725} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac7912da-4019-572a-975e-35b8a1f7cc4e" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F=$ $\\left(- 4 x y^{3} + 2 x - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf i$ $+\\left(- 9 x^{2} y^{2} + 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718741} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64eba286-fa17-5b4b-84b8-6d67b6081d15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718727} {:answer/id #uuid "c3af32c0-ff81-53ae-94cb-97a6cd623c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718746}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3af32c0-ff81-53ae-94cb-97a6cd623c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718746} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad374b2e-1f55-50ec-a9f7-cc8cea9e5593" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718742} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d35de68-244d-517f-b3c1-9ab55f360c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718719} {:answer/id #uuid "cc4eb702-e5a5-5ad0-a551-4b8ef9d819a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d35de68-244d-517f-b3c1-9ab55f360c75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718719} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd3d893b-c0e9-5c9b-b4b8-35fc4f8b657c" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf H=$ $\\left(4 x y^{3} - 2 x\\right)\\,\\mathbf i$ $+\\left(6 x^{2} y^{2} - 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718751}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3ca20335-a76b-5b45-82cd-c34a8fc147a5" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on $\\mathbb R^2$? Select all that apply.\n\nFor $\\mathbf V=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$ with continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$, the field is conservative exactly when $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere. The partial derivatives are supplied:\n\n| Field | $P_y$ | $Q_x$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\mathbf F$ | $- 12 x y^{2}$ | $- 18 x y^{2}$ |\n| $\\mathbf G$ | $2 x$ | $- 2 x$ |\n| $\\mathbf H$ | $12 x y^{2}$ | $12 x y^{2}$ |" :question/worked-solution "All components have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. Polynomial, exponential, trigonometric and arctangent functions are smooth here; any logarithm has positive argument and any denominator is strictly positive. Thus $\\mathbf V=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$ is **conservative** exactly when $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere.\n\nFor $\\mathbf F$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=- 4 x y^{3} + 2 x - 1,\\\\Q&=- 9 x^{2} y^{2} + 2 y,\\\\P_y&=- 12 x y^{2},\\\\Q_x&=- 18 x y^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivatives are not equal everywhere, so $\\mathbf F$ is not conservative. At $(1,1)$, the difference is $6\\ne0$.\n\nFor $\\mathbf G$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=2 x y + 2 x,\\\\Q&=- x^{2} + 2 y - 1,\\\\P_y&=2 x,\\\\Q_x&=- 2 x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivatives are not equal everywhere, so $\\mathbf G$ is not conservative. At $(1,0)$, the difference is $4\\ne0$.\n\nFor $\\mathbf H$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=4 x y^{3} - 2 x,\\\\Q&=6 x^{2} y^{2} - 2 y,\\\\P_y&=12 x y^{2},\\\\Q_x&=12 x y^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$P_y=Q_x$ is an identity, so $\\mathbf H$ is conservative.\n\nSelect $\\mathbf H$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718739 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fb210c6-9da3-5b75-b169-843a52774bc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718723} {:answer/id #uuid "fb42e92a-4355-5af0-a9ab-a2c1cda6a6a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb42e92a-4355-5af0-a9ab-a2c1cda6a6a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718757} :answer-field/id #uuid "06ac7a05-c768-54ba-b9ec-88b743261465" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf H=$ $\\left(4 x y^{2} - x - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf i$ $+\\left(- 4 x^{2} y - y - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718708} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67de3cd1-8fe2-51cf-991b-afc21ccc1444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718728} {:answer/id #uuid "f6455dde-fe67-55e7-abe7-b0d9fa02f61c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67de3cd1-8fe2-51cf-991b-afc21ccc1444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718728} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a7d8e4e-ee03-5aaf-84ec-bb1ad6ce419a" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718711} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1defda75-8090-54a2-9f51-65f232b06fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718713} {:answer/id #uuid "fa00232c-908e-580f-a117-55c0eac01a4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1defda75-8090-54a2-9f51-65f232b06fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718713} :answer-field/id #uuid "9911c4d6-423b-56ee-9df6-7a7ea250b65f" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf G=$ $\\left(- 2 x + y\\right)\\,\\mathbf i$ $+\\left(2 x - 2 y - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718736} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "447dc6a8-af69-5512-8b17-8a0e13061073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718721} {:answer/id #uuid "792a8554-a42f-5b56-99ed-aeeabc04ea8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "792a8554-a42f-5b56-99ed-aeeabc04ea8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718731} :answer-field/id #uuid "d52087e6-8128-5140-b734-3126c29e85e5" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F=$ $\\left(x - y\\right)\\,\\mathbf i$ $+\\left(3 x + y\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718749}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9dfa9a3e-bd5e-54ea-ac88-ebd2b57d112b" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on $\\mathbb R^2$? Select all that apply.\n\nFor $\\mathbf V=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$ with continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$, the field is conservative exactly when $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere. The partial derivatives are supplied:\n\n| Field | $P_y$ | $Q_x$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\mathbf F$ | $-1$ | $3$ |\n| $\\mathbf G$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| $\\mathbf H$ | $8 x y$ | $- 8 x y$ |" :question/worked-solution "All components have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. Polynomial, exponential, trigonometric and arctangent functions are smooth here; any logarithm has positive argument and any denominator is strictly positive. Thus $\\mathbf V=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$ is **conservative** exactly when $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere.\n\nFor $\\mathbf F$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=x - y,\\\\Q&=3 x + y,\\\\P_y&=-1,\\\\Q_x&=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivatives are not equal everywhere, so $\\mathbf F$ is not conservative. At $(0,0)$, the difference is $-4\\ne0$.\n\nFor $\\mathbf G$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=- 2 x + y,\\\\Q&=2 x - 2 y - 1,\\\\P_y&=1,\\\\Q_x&=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivatives are not equal everywhere, so $\\mathbf G$ is not conservative. At $(0,0)$, the difference is $-1\\ne0$.\n\nFor $\\mathbf H$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=4 x y^{2} - x - 1,\\\\Q&=- 4 x^{2} y - y - 1,\\\\P_y&=8 x y,\\\\Q_x&=- 8 x y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivatives are not equal everywhere, so $\\mathbf H$ is not conservative. At $(1,1)$, the difference is $16\\ne0$.\n\nSelect **None of the above**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718750 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29343991-24ce-5d8f-9611-4bbb0578eb92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718716} {:answer/id #uuid "cf7f8fb8-a36b-5522-b6b3-6c086d31a139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29343991-24ce-5d8f-9611-4bbb0578eb92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718716} :answer-field/id #uuid "0393439b-dd9e-50dc-9cf3-5fc708842b05" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F=$ $\\left(x - 2 y + 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf i$ $+\\left(- 2 x + y + 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718707} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99ae86aa-cb6b-526a-ac98-750a63f31e59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718737} {:answer/id #uuid "c11f1972-827d-5305-ab92-915ea571371d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99ae86aa-cb6b-526a-ac98-750a63f31e59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718737} :answer-field/id #uuid "0918bd93-ce33-5f1d-936c-dad0ae553325" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718709} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00786252-6b4d-51ed-825d-8e3d67660818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718706} {:answer/id #uuid "f83d893e-6361-51fb-a28f-eb1816475273" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f83d893e-6361-51fb-a28f-eb1816475273" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718755} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa3a4ae5-fe07-55ee-ad49-e3e81fd35cae" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf G=$ $\\left(- 2 x + y + 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf i$ $+\\left(- 2 x - 2 y - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718740} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dcc7e62-0823-5bc3-b534-7556ad3392c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718712} {:answer/id #uuid "8e1da421-7b1a-53c0-8cfb-b387df60a5d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e1da421-7b1a-53c0-8cfb-b387df60a5d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718732} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec8934c3-d1d4-5c5d-96ce-22583964081e" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf H=$ $\\left(2 x - 1\\right)\\,\\mathbf i$ $+\\left(2 x + 2 y\\right)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718753}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da4b13f3-6244-5171-bc57-e41231c2cf6d" :question/problem "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on $\\mathbb R^2$? Select all that apply.\n\nFor $\\mathbf V=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$ with continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$, the field is conservative exactly when $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere. The partial derivatives are supplied:\n\n| Field | $P_y$ | $Q_x$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\mathbf F$ | $-2$ | $-2$ |\n| $\\mathbf G$ | $1$ | $-2$ |\n| $\\mathbf H$ | $0$ | $2$ |" :question/worked-solution "All components have continuous first partial derivatives on $\\mathbb R^2$. Polynomial, exponential, trigonometric and arctangent functions are smooth here; any logarithm has positive argument and any denominator is strictly positive. Thus $\\mathbf V=P\\,\\mathbf i+Q\\,\\mathbf j$ is **conservative** exactly when $P_y=Q_x$ everywhere.\n\nFor $\\mathbf F$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=x - 2 y + 1,\\\\Q&=- 2 x + y + 1,\\\\P_y&=-2,\\\\Q_x&=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$P_y=Q_x$ is an identity, so $\\mathbf F$ is conservative.\n\nFor $\\mathbf G$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=- 2 x + y + 1,\\\\Q&=- 2 x - 2 y - 1,\\\\P_y&=1,\\\\Q_x&=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivatives are not equal everywhere, so $\\mathbf G$ is not conservative. At $(0,0)$, the difference is $3\\ne0$.\n\nFor $\\mathbf H$, differentiate each component with respect to the indicated variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P&=2 x - 1,\\\\Q&=2 x + 2 y,\\\\P_y&=0,\\\\Q_x&=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivatives are not equal everywhere, so $\\mathbf H$ is not conservative. At $(0,0)$, the difference is $-2\\ne0$.\n\nSelect $\\mathbf F$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7180dc2d-ab6b-57ae-b7d0-f54371862397" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(4 s - 3\\right) e^{s^{2} - 2 s + 3 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718817} {:answer/id #uuid "72f58770-7d8e-5eb2-b008-ef5a144566e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\left(s + 1\\right) e^{s^{2} - 2 s + 3 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718818} {:answer/id #uuid "c863138c-2ce5-51da-a638-883109fe30fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(2 s - 3\\right) e^{s^{2} - 2 s + 3 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718829} {:answer/id #uuid "ef0fa5a5-57f4-50e1-b624-417803e2f75b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 s e^{s^{2} - 2 s + 3 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718835} {:answer/id #uuid "f8817599-03b9-5a60-a56c-97649f70e395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\left(s - 1\\right) e^{s^{2} - 2 s + 3 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8817599-03b9-5a60-a56c-97649f70e395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\left(s - 1\\right) e^{s^{2} - 2 s + 3 t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718837} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e49c2eb-5e59-56db-9129-42e5e1738901" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8975c4ac-80eb-5545-bc60-3ea616b6c93a" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=e^{x + y + z}$, where $x=- s + 2 t$, $y=s^{2}$, $z=- s + t$. Calculate $\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}$ in terms of $s$ and $t$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nHold $t$ fixed. Multiply along the three paths and add:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\cdot \\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial s}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\cdot \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial s}+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\cdot \\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial s}\n$$\n\nFirst find the outer partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=e^{x + y + z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=e^{x + y + z} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=e^{x + y + z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite these partials in terms of $s$ and $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}&=e^{s^{2} - 2 s + 3 t} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}&=e^{s^{2} - 2 s + 3 t} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}&=e^{s^{2} - 2 s + 3 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiate each intermediate variable with respect to $s$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial s}&=-1 \\\\ \\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial s}&=2 s \\\\ \\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial s}&=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute the matching factors, then collect terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial s}&=\\left(e^{s^{2} - 2 s + 3 t}\\right)\\left(-1\\right) \\\\ &{}+\\left(e^{s^{2} - 2 s + 3 t}\\right)\\left(2 s\\right) \\\\ &{}+\\left(e^{s^{2} - 2 s + 3 t}\\right)\\left(-1\\right) \\\\ &=2 \\left(s - 1\\right) e^{s^{2} - 2 s + 3 t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"}]}
